 "notes": "Crocodile Rock, a low rock about 190 m off the Dwejra shore between the Blue Hole and Fungus Rock, with the shallow plateau towards the shore, the cut-out to its south and the wall around it. The rock outline is approximate (it is not in OpenStreetMap); the coastline and Fungus Rock are from OSM. Layout and depths follow the St Andrew's Divers Cove (gozodive.com) site description, whose boat anchors on the plateau; the plateau extent and wall line are approximate. The site coordinates in the data point at the land; the rock is at about 36.0503, 14.1869, which is used as the map origin.",
